# ⚡ NeonLedger — AI Finance Controller

### Verification-first AI for finance operations

> **Close the books faster. Trust the numbers more. Know what the AI couldn't resolve.**

[![Live Demo](https://img.shields.io/badge/Live%20Demo-NeonLedger-00D4FF?style=for-the-badge)](https://ai-finance-controller-jade.vercel.app/)
[![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-Prototype-success?style=for-the-badge)](#)
[![Finance AI](https://img.shields.io/badge/Domain-Finance%20AI-purple?style=for-the-badge)](#)
[![Verification First](https://img.shields.io/badge/Philosophy-Verification%20First-orange?style=for-the-badge)](#)

**NeonLedger** is a verification-first AI Finance Controller designed to close one of the most repetitive and error-prone finance-operations loops: **multi-source reconciliation**.

It processes a batch of synthetic financial records spanning invoices, bank transactions, settlement records, and tax lines, determines which records can be safely reconciled, measures the result, and exposes unresolved exceptions instead of hiding them behind a misleading 100% automation claim.

---

## 🚀 Live Demo

### [▶ Launch NeonLedger](https://ai-finance-controller-jade.vercel.app/)

The demo provides an interactive finance-control workspace for:

* Running a reconciliation batch
* Inspecting match decisions
* Reviewing unresolved exceptions
* Understanding settlement discrepancies
* Monitoring cash impact
* Asking finance-oriented questions
* Adjusting confidence thresholds
* Evaluating batch-level results

---

# 🎯 Problem

Finance teams still spend significant operational effort reconciling information that exists across disconnected systems.

A single business transaction can appear as:

```text
Invoice
   │
   ├──────────────► Bank transaction
   │
   ├──────────────► Payment gateway settlement
   │
   └──────────────► Tax record
```

The identifiers may differ.

Descriptions may be inconsistent.

Settlement fees may change the net amount.

Tax records may be missing or incorrect.

Chargebacks and duplicate deposits can introduce additional risk.

The dangerous solution is to simply maximize the number of matches.

The better solution is:

> **Match what can be verified. Escalate what cannot. Measure both.**

---

# 💡 What NeonLedger Solves

NeonLedger closes a complete finance-operations reconciliation loop:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              MULTI-SOURCE DATA              │
│                                             │
│  Invoices │ Bank │ Settlements │ Tax Lines │
└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                 NORMALIZE                   │
│                                             │
│ IDs • dates • amounts • references • names  │
└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│             CANDIDATE MATCHING              │
│                                             │
│ Amount • Date • Reference • Entity • Fees   │
└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                AI REASONING                 │
│                                             │
│ Ambiguity • discrepancy • exception cause   │
└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           DETERMINISTIC VERIFICATION        │
│                                             │
│ Tolerances • arithmetic • duplicates • tax  │
└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                       │
              ┌────────┴────────┐
              ▼                 ▼
       ┌─────────────┐   ┌───────────────┐
       │   AUTO-CLOSE │   │   EXCEPTION   │
       └──────┬──────┘   └───────┬───────┘
              │                  │
              ▼                  ▼
       Cash Position       Human Review
       + Audit Trail       + Explanation
```

---

# 📊 Demo Dataset

The current demonstration processes **94 synthetic financial records** across multiple finance sources:

| Source             | Records |
| ------------------ | ------: |
| Invoices           |      24 |
| Bank transactions  |      24 |
| Settlement records |      24 |
| Tax records        |      22 |
| **Total**          |  **94** |

The dataset intentionally contains both valid relationships and problematic records.

Examples include:

* Missing invoices
* Duplicate deposits
* Chargeback reversals
* Unknown bank sweeps
* Settlement discrepancies
* Tax mismatches
* Missing tax lines

This prevents the system from simply producing a perfect score on a perfectly clean dataset.

---

# 🧠 Verification-First Architecture

The central design principle is:

> **AI proposes and explains. Deterministic controls verify.**

Financial arithmetic should not depend on an LLM's ability to perform calculations reliably.

NeonLedger separates reasoning from verification.

### AI / Reasoning Layer

Useful for:

* Entity resolution
* Interpreting inconsistent descriptions
* Ranking possible matches
* Explaining discrepancies
* Classifying exception causes
* Generating investigation recommendations
* Answering natural-language finance questions

### Deterministic Control Layer

Responsible for:

* Amount validation
* Currency consistency
* Date tolerances
* Settlement fee calculations
* Tax calculations
* Duplicate detection
* Confidence thresholds
* Ledger consistency

This hybrid approach makes the system more suitable for finance workflows than an LLM-only architecture.

---

# 🔍 Reconciliation Logic

A transaction is not considered safely matched merely because two records look similar.

The system evaluates multiple pieces of evidence:

```text
                    Candidate Match
                          │
             ┌────────────┼────────────┐
             ▼            ▼            ▼
          Amount         Date       Reference
             │            │            │
             └────────────┼────────────┘
                          ▼
                  Evidence Score
                          │
                          ▼
                Verification Rules
                          │
               ┌──────────┴──────────┐
               ▼                     ▼
          AUTO-MATCH             EXCEPTION
```

Example:

```text
Invoice
INV-6407
Amount: $4,182

Bank
BNK-9107
Amount: $4,182

Settlement
SET-7307
Net: $4,182

Tax
TAX-5207
Tax: $342

                ↓

All evidence consistent

                ↓

        VERIFIED MATCH
```

While an inconsistent transaction becomes:

```text
Invoice
      ↓
Candidate Bank Transaction
      ↓
Amount mismatch
      ↓
Settlement discrepancy
      ↓
Tax inconsistency

                ↓

           EXCEPTION
```

The system deliberately avoids forcing the second transaction into a match.

---

# 📈 What Is Measured?

The project is designed around measurable outcomes rather than a single cherry-picked successful transaction.

### Throughput

```text
Records processed
─────────────────
Processing time
```

### Match Rate

```text
Successfully matched records
─────────────────────────────
Eligible records
```

### Precision

```text
Correct matches
────────────────
Predicted matches
```

### Recall

```text
Correct matches
────────────────
All valid matches
```

### Exception Quality

```text
Correctly identified exceptions
───────────────────────────────
All flagged exceptions
```

### Cash Impact

The controller also surfaces how unresolved reconciliation issues affect the observed and expected cash position.

---

# 🚨 Exception-First Design

A finance controller should not hide uncertainty.

NeonLedger explicitly surfaces exceptions such as:

| Exception           | Example Risk                |
| ------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Missing invoice     | Unknown cash allocation     |
| Duplicate deposit   | Potential double counting   |
| Chargeback          | Negative cash impact        |
| Tax mismatch        | Compliance / reporting risk |
| Settlement mismatch | Incorrect expected cash     |
| Unknown bank sweep  | Unexplained movement        |

Each exception can be investigated rather than silently classified as a successful match.

---

# 💬 Finance Q&A

The controller is also designed as a natural-language interface over the reconciliation state.

Example questions:

```text
Why were these items unmatched?

What threatens cash this week?

Which settlements have discrepancies?

Which tax lines need review?

Show me the highest-risk exceptions.

Why did this transaction fail reconciliation?
```

A production implementation can ground these responses in structured finance tools rather than allowing the model to invent financial facts.

