# 🔐 Why Not Let an LLM Decide Everything?

Because financial correctness matters more than conversational fluency.

An LLM can be excellent at:

> "These two messy transaction descriptions probably refer to the same customer."

But it should not be trusted to independently decide:

> "These two ledger amounts balance."

That calculation should be deterministic.

Therefore:

```text
              AI
               │
        Reason / Explain
               │
               ▼
        Candidate Decision
               │
               ▼
      Deterministic Controls
               │
        ┌──────┴──────┐
        ▼             ▼
     Verified      Exception
```

This is the core philosophy behind NeonLedger.

---

# 🧪 Synthetic Data & Evaluation

The project uses synthetic financial data so that the complete reconciliation process can be evaluated against known expected outcomes without exposing real financial information.

A stronger production evaluation setup uses a hidden ground-truth layer:

```text
Generated Record
       │
       ├── Actual relationship
       │
       ├── Expected decision
       │
       └── Expected exception type
                │
                ▼
          Agent Decision
                │
                ▼
           Evaluation
                │
       ┌────────┼────────┐
       ▼        ▼        ▼
   Precision   Recall   Exceptions
```

This makes it possible to distinguish:

**"The system found a match."**

from:

**"The system found the correct match."**

